# Copy to .env. Expo only exposes vars prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to the client.

# The API the app talks to. There is no mock mode: every screen reads and
# writes the real database, so this must resolve to a running server.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET for local development. With no value, the app derives the
# API host from the dev server the bundle came from - a phone that reached
# Metro on 172.20.10.11:8081 reaches the API on 172.20.10.11:4000 - so it
# follows the machine onto a new network by itself.
#
# A pinned IP here does the opposite. It survives the network change that
# invalidated it, and an address on a subnet the phone can no longer route to
# does not fail: it hangs, with no reply to reject, until the request times
# out. That is what once left every screen spinning on Expo Go.
#
# Set it only to point at a server that is genuinely somewhere else - a staging
# or production API. Then it is a real choice rather than a stale note.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api
